                <pb facs="0751" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/2052: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden (Johnson) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-04T12:00:00+01:00">March 4,
                            1942—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 4—11:41 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>415. Department’s 121, March 3, 8 p.m. Among suggestions made by British
                    Government regarding relief for Greece was one to effect that proposal as far as
                    Germans concerned should appear to come from Swedish initiative and that if
                    possible Germans should not be allowed to know of British-American action.
                    Boheman agreed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
